{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01Gos27f1zxBM5HNKEAChpUV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01TvU2BuX96tjT18VfHuqbBs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"conda run -n wave python3 -c \"\nimport sympy as sp\n\nx, t = sp.symbols('x t', real=True, nonnegative=True)\nc = sp.symbols('c', positive=True)\nT_sym = sp.symbols('T', positive=True)\nN, k = sp.symbols('N k', positive=True)\n\n# For the double-log ansatz psi = -log(1+t) - log(1+x), alpha=1, lam=-1/N:\n# The L2 expression (after normalization) is a quadratic in z = c^2(1+t)^2/(1+x)^2\n# with z^2 coefficient: A_coeff - B_coeff * R\n# where R = ((1+t)(1+x))^(2/N)\n#\n# The key insight from round 4 report:\n# - s only appears in L2\n# - L, L1, phi_xt do NOT depend on s\n# - So conditions 1, 2, sufficient are unaffected by choice of s\n#\n# The L2 operator has structure:\n#   L2 = (1/2)*(alpha-1)*s*lam*square(phi*square(psi)) - (1/2)*s*lam^2*square(phi*tilde_square(psi))\n#        + s^3*lam^3*(alpha-1)*phi^3*tilde_square(psi)*square(psi)\n#        - s^3*lam^4*phi^3*tilde_square(psi)^2\n#        + s^3*lam^3*(div terms)\n#\n# With alpha=1, the (alpha-1) terms vanish, so:\n#   L2 = -(1/2)*s*lam^2*square(phi*tilde_square(psi))\n#        - s^3*lam^4*phi^3*tilde_square(psi)^2\n#        + s^3*lam^3*(div terms)\n#\n# The first term is O(s) = O(|s|) (positive since s<0, lam^2>0, and for double-log square(phi*tilde) < 0)\n# The last two terms are O(s^3) = O(|s|^3)\n#\n# For s = -1/(c^k * (1+T)^m), the threshold becomes:\n# R_max = (c*(1+T)^2)^(2/N), and we need R_max < f_min ~ 1/s^2 = c^{2k}*(1+T)^{2m}\n# => (c*(1+T)^2)^(2/N) < c^{2k}*(1+T)^{2m}\n# => c^{2/N}*(1+T)^{4/N} < c^{2k}*(1+T)^{2m}\n#\n# This needs: 2k > 2/N (for c exponent) AND 2m > 4/N (for T exponent)\n# So k > 1/N and m > 2/N\n#\n# With N=20 (lam=-1/20): k > 1/20 = 0.05, m > 2/20 = 0.1\n# Let's use k=1, m=1 for simplicity: s = -1/(c*(1+T))\n# Then: c^{2/20} < c^2 needs c>1 (NOT all c)\n# Actually we need this for ALL c > 0 including c < 1\n\n# Hmm, let's think more carefully. The condition is:\n# R_max^{N/2} < f_min^{N/2} where:\n# R_max^{N/2} = c*(1+T)^2  (since R_max = (c*(1+T)^2)^(2/N), and N/2 * 2/N = 1)\n# f_min ~ C * (1/|s|^2) for some constant C independent of c,T\n# So we need: c*(1+T)^2 < C * (1/|s|^2)\n# => |s|^2 < C/(c*(1+T)^2)\n# => |s| < sqrt(C/(c*(1+T)^2)) = sqrt(C) / sqrt(c*(1+T)^2)\n# So set s = -1/sqrt(c*(1+T)^2) = -1/(sqrt(c)*(1+T))\n\n# But wait, f_min depends on the L2 coefficients which involve s and N.\n# Let me be more precise.\n\n# From the round 4 report:\n# A(z) = 5752500*z^2 + 95000*z + 5752500  (with s=-1/100, N=20)\n# B(z) = 28*z^2 + z - 29\n# f_min = min_{z>1} A(z)/B(z) = 205437\n#\n# With s = -sigma (sigma > 0), the A and B coefficients scale as:\n# Term_B (O(s)) contributes to A: proportional to |s| = sigma\n# Term_D,E (O(s^3)) contribute to B: proportional to sigma^3\n# So A ~ C1 * sigma, B ~ C2 * sigma^3\n# f_min ~ A/B ~ C1/(C2*sigma^2) = C3/sigma^2\n#\n# We need R_max < f_min, i.e., (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/10) < C3/sigma^2\n# => sigma^2 < C3 / (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/10)\n# => sigma < sqrt(C3) / (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/20)\n# So s = -K / (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/20) for some constant K > 0\n\nprint('Scaling analysis:')\nprint('  Need sigma^2 * R_max < C3')\nprint('  R_max = (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/10)')\nprint('  So sigma < K / (c*(1+T)^2)^(1/20)')\nprint()\nprint('Choosing s = -1/(c*(1+T)^2)^(1/20) should work.')\nprint('Or more conservatively s = -1/(c^2 * (1+T)^4)^(1/20) = -1/(c*(1+T)^2)^(1/10)')\nprint()\nprint('Simplest: s = -c^(-1/10) works if we only need c-dependence.')\nprint('With T: s = -1/(c*(1+T)^2)^(1/10)')\n\"\n","description":"Analyze scaling for s depending on c"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":298,"cache_read_input_tokens":117248,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":298,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0b1db25-cef4-4434-ae8d-fa0fa5f67b93","uuid":"1d62f155-7397-49ff-bef2-5d0ba023a16e"}
