getting complex. Let me try alpha=0.\n# With alpha=0: (alpha-1) = -1\n# L = lam^2*phi*tilde_sq + lam*phi*box_psi = lam*phi*(lam*tilde_sq + box_psi)\n# For double-log: tilde_sq = box_psi, so L = lam*phi*(lam+1)*box_psi\n\n# Condition 1a: L - L1 >= 0\n# L/phi = lam*(lam+1)*box_psi, L1/phi = lam^2*P + lam*Q where P = psi_t^2+c^2*psi_x^2\n# For double-log: P = Q (the self-similar property!), so L1/phi = lam(lam+1)*P\n# And box_psi = tilde_sq = psi_t^2 - c^2*psi_x^2\n# P = psi_t^2 + c^2*psi_x^2\n# L - L1 = phi*lam*(lam+1)*(box_psi - P) = phi*lam*(lam+1)*(-2c^2*psi_x^2)\n# With lam < 0, lam+1 > 0 (for |lam| < 1): lam*(lam+1) < 0\n# -2c^2*psi_x^2 < 0\n# Product of two negatives = positive. L-L1 >= 0 ✓\n\n# Same structure as alpha=1 for condition 1 (the conditions 1a, 1b don't depend on alpha\n# for the double-log since box_psi = tilde_sq).\n\n# But condition 3 (L2) DOES change with alpha.\n# The additional L2 term from (alpha-1):\n# (alpha-1)/2 * s*lam * square(phi*box_psi)\n# With alpha=0, (alpha-1) = -1:\n# -1/2 * s*lam * square(phi*box_psi)\n# = sigma/(2N) * square(phi*box_psi)  [since s=-sigma, lam=-1/N]\n# This is the SAME as the existing term -(s/2)*lam^2*square(phi*tilde_sq) \n# multiplied by N (since box_psi = tilde_sq for double-log).\n# Wait no: -(s/2)*lam^2 = sigma/(2N^2), and -(alpha-1)*s*lam/2 = sigma/(2N)\n# So the new term is N times larger! This could help.\n\n# With alpha=0, the total O(sigma) coefficient is:\n# sigma/(2N^2)*square(phi*tilde_sq) + sigma/(2N)*square(phi*tilde_sq)  \n# = sigma*(N+1)/(2N^2)*square(phi*tilde_sq)\n# This is about N times larger than with alpha=1. The O(sigma^3) terms also change\n# because of the new s^3*lam^3*(alpha-1)*phi^3*tilde_sq*box_psi term.\n\n# For double-log: (alpha-1)*tilde_sq*box_psi = -tilde_sq^2\n# So: s^3*lam^3*(alpha-1)*phi^3*tilde_sq*box_psi = -s^3*lam^3*phi^3*tilde_sq^2\n# = -(-sigma)^3*(-1/N)^3*phi^3*tilde_sq^2 = sigma^3/N^3*phi^3*tilde_sq^2\n\n# And the existing: -s^3*lam^4*phi^3*tilde_sq^2 = sigma^3/N^4*phi