{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_bdrk_01Tyoo3QVFMHPL9nzR8oJ1re","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01MiJFHQT6ScbhHg2qv6ZHkk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/cyanz/wave_PINN/candidates/round_5/candidate.py","content":"# Description: Double-logarithm ansatz with c-dependent s to fix L₂\n#\n# SAME functional form as Rounds 2-4: ψ = -log(1+t) - log(1+x)\n# but with s = -1/c (a function of c, as the problem explicitly allows).\n#\n# KEY INSIGHT (from Round 4 failure analysis):\n# The L₂ condition fails because the \"R-growing\" phi^3 terms eventually\n# dominate the \"constant\" phi terms. With fixed s = -sigma (constant):\n#   L₂ = sigma * (positive O(1) term) - sigma^3 * (R-dependent term)\n# where R = ((1+t)(1+x))^(1/10).\n# With s = -1/c (sigma = 1/c), the O(sigma^3) term scales as 1/c^3,\n# while the O(sigma) term scales as 1/c.\n#\n# On the actual problem domain [0,∞) × [0,T] for given c, T:\n# - In the z ≤ 1 region (where (1+x) ≥ c(1+t)): L₂ > 0 always (B(z) ≤ 0)\n# - In the z > 1 region: (1+x) < c(1+T), so (1+t)(1+x) < c(1+T)²\n#   and R < (c(1+T)²)^(1/10) = R_max(c,T)\n#   The threshold is f_min ~ C₃/sigma² = C₃·c²\n#   Need R_max < f_min: (c(1+T)²)^(1/10) < C₃·c²\n#   i.e., c^(1/10)·(1+T)^(1/5) < C₃·c², which holds for all c > 0 when c is large,\n#   and for small c the R_max is small. Specifically:\n#   c^(1/10)/(c^2) = c^(-19/10) → 0 as c → ∞, so the condition is satisfied for large c.\n#   For small c (c → 0): R_max → 0 and f_min → ∞, trivially satisfied.\n#\n# Conditions 1, 2, and the sufficient condition are IDENTICAL to Rounds 2-4\n# (they don't depend on s at all), and were proven true in Rounds 2-4.\n#\n# Properties (unchanged from Rounds 2-4):\n# - Self-similar: P = Q, tilde_sq = box_psi\n# - With alpha=1, lam=-1/20: L₁/φ = (-19/400)·P < 0 ✓\n# - Condition 1a: sum of positive terms ✓\n# - Condition 1b: sum of positive terms ✓\n# - Condition 2: λψ = (1/20)·log((1+t)(1+x)) → +∞ ✓\n# - Sufficient: quadratic with no positive roots ✓\n\npsi = -sp.ln(1 + t) - sp.ln(1 + x)\n\nsubs_dict = {\n    alpha : 1,\n    s     : -1 / c,\n    lam   : sp.Rational(-1, 20),\n}\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":182219,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":483,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0b1db25-cef4-4434-ae8d-fa0fa5f67b93","uuid":"c593c6e4-5daf-4fa6-b72a-15fdd9048023"}
